# ============================================================================
# Code Owners
# ============================================================================
# GitHub requests a review from the owners below on any pull request that
# touches the matching paths. The review only becomes mandatory when the
# repository's branch ruleset enables "Require review from Code Owners".
#
# Scope is intentionally narrow: only the security-sensitive paths that could
# change what CI enforces, who can release, which dependencies are allowed, or
# which dependency updates merge without review. Everything else follows the
# normal pull request flow.
# ============================================================================

# All GitHub Actions workflows - a change here can weaken the CI gate or alter
# who can release.
/.github/workflows/   @fulviofreitas

# This file itself - prevent removing the owner rule via a sneaky PR.
/.github/CODEOWNERS   @fulviofreitas

# Renovate config - controls which dependency updates auto-merge and at what
# cadence; loosening it could land an unreviewed compromised package.
/.github/renovate.json5   @fulviofreitas

# CI-enforced policy and release behaviour: deny.toml is the supply-chain gate
# (allowed git sources, advisory ignores); .releaserc.json runs shell commands in
# the release job; commitlint.config.js decides which commits pass; and
# rust-toolchain.toml selects the toolchain CI builds with.
/deny.toml              @fulviofreitas
/.releaserc.json        @fulviofreitas
/commitlint.config.js   @fulviofreitas
/rust-toolchain.toml    @fulviofreitas

# The files that enforce the read-only and secret-safety guarantees: the guard test (banned
# and allowed lists, pinned exceptions), the hygiene test, the harness that mounts the write
# tripwire, the redaction deny-list and the error mapping. Weakening any of them would let a
# write path or a leaked secret through with a green build.
/tests/read_only_guard.rs   @fulviofreitas
/tests/public_hygiene.rs    @fulviofreitas
/tests/common/mod.rs        @fulviofreitas
/src/redact.rs              @fulviofreitas
/src/errors.rs              @fulviofreitas
